   "brief": "Portvell, a river port. A wide river (one seventh of the image wide) crosses the image from left to right a little below the middle. Along the north bank, a long grey quay with five short brown wooden piers sticking into the water; three cyan warehouses and one orange exchange hall stand on the waterfront. One grey stone bridge crosses to a small quarter of scattered houses on the south bank. An irregular beige market square in the middle of the town, near the river. About 90 small red houses packed tightly in irregular blocks between curving streets. Two grey roads leave the town to the left and to the right edges of the image. Yellow fields and dark green woods at the edges. No town wall."
