   "brief": "Bellcaire, a walled market city on a wide river. A wide blue river crosses the bottom fifth of the image from left to right. A black town wall with small square towers makes a rough oval around the old town, from the river bank round the north back to the river bank, with four gates where the main roads pass. Inside: an irregular beige market square in the middle, a large purple cathedral with a small beige square in front of it beside the market square, about 250 small red houses packed in irregular blocks, narrow alleys. On the river bank inside the wall: a grey quay with six brown piers, an orange exchange hall and three cyan warehouses. One grey bridge crosses the river to a loose suburb of red houses on the far bank; another loose suburb outside the west gate. Grey roads leave from each gate to the edges. Yellow fields and dark green woods around."
  },
