   "brief": "Peñarroja, a mining and quarry village at the foot of a mountain. The top fifth of the image is bare rock of the mountain (dark brownish grey) with a ragged edge. A narrow blue torrent comes down from the rock and runs to the bottom edge, crossed by one grey bridge. A small beige square in the middle; about 40 small red stone houses in short irregular rows along the curving lanes, climbing towards the rock. At the foot of the rock: a magenta mine entrance at the end of a lane, a very light grey quarry pit cut into the rock on the left. Grey roads to the left, right and bottom edges; a few yellow fields to the south, dark green woods."
